{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>How can I bear alone your burden.</b> The burden that is upon me, that I make the commandments understandable to the simple. And our Rabbis, of blessed memory, interpreted: this teaches that Israel were great complainers — one of them, seeing his opponent prevail in judgment, would say, 'I have witnesses to bring, I have proof to bring' —מוסיפני עליכם דיינין ('I impose upon you [the need for more] judges')." "<b>And your load.</b> When they demanded the meat and the water, as it is written (Numbers 11:11): לשום את משא כל העם הזה עלי." "<b>And your disputes.</b> This teaches you that they were men of strife and quarrel, one with another."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:44:30.880208335Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}